# Line endings are load-bearing here.
#
# The repo is authored on Windows but the shell scripts run on Raspberry
# Pi OS. A CRLF line ending makes bash fail with errors like
#   syntax error near unexpected token `$'in\r''
# so every text file is stored AND checked out with LF, on every
# platform. Without this, a Windows clone produces scripts that cannot
# run on the Pi.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
# Fonts are vendored; `text=auto` detects them correctly today, but a
# webfont mangled by an eol conversion fails silently — the board just
# renders in a fallback face — so say it outright.
*.woff2 binary
